      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It won’t really work, especially since more and more countries around the world are trying to introduce age restrictions for online services. These regulations usually all have the same core idea: verify the user’s personal data.\n\nAn account itself could already be 18 years old, which would mean you know the person is an adult. Lawmakers still require a separate verification, though.\n\nSo it doesn’t make any sense to build a system now that relies on the age of the account.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
